{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation pushed for review: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2263 (\"Detect orphaned high-CPU agent helpers\").\n\nThree files, exactly the recorded file_impact:\n- AGENTS.md — new section \"Bound every background process you spawn — never leave a PPID-1 orphan\": bound-at-spawn (`timeout 120 python -c 'while True: pass' &`), process-group teardown (`trap 'kill 0' EXIT INT TERM`), the reap-including-error-paths and no-PPID-1 rules, why an unbounded loop outlives harness death, and the operator note (`pgrep -fl` then `pkill -f 'while True: pass'`, which cleared this host's 38).\n- scripts/check_orphaned_load.py — on-demand detector, PPID == 1 AND cpu_seconds > 3600 (default, `--min-cpu-seconds` overrides). Read-only; never signals. Deliberately not wired into `make lint` (it reports live host state, not the tree under review), so no CI-provider dependency.\n- tests/scripts/test_check_orphaned_load.py — 18 tests over an injected process-lister seam plus one read-only live-adapter smoke assertion. No test spawns a CPU burner.\n\nRED->GREEN: test module written first, failed 18/18 on the missing module, then 18/18 green.\n\nDefect-seeded mutations, all killed: (1) drop the PPID-1 condition -> 2 failures; (2) flip `>` to `<` -> 7 failures; (3) default 3600 -> 60 -> 2 failures; (4) real adapter stops excluding self -> 1 failure.\n\nGates: make lint 0, make typecheck 0, check_complexity_baseline --check 0 (new=0 increased=0), check_import_walk 0, check_commit_message_wrap 0, and the 290 tests that read AGENTS.md all pass.\n\nNot closing — awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 on 2263."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787814440327618406,"uuid":"0946ec22-3933-410b-9709-d5f904459728"}